    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** pacing the offense at an elite 82.97 efficiency score. Facing Keider Montero in a favorable park environment, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a robust 0.448 xwOBA and a strong +8% order premium as the projected number two hitter. He is joined at the top of our lineup by **Christian Yelich** (75.84), who draws a high-value matchup against Colin Rea. While **Christian Yelich** faces a slight negative hold on stolen base attempts, his +13% platoon edge and top-of-the-order positioning make him a primary engine for our Roto categories today. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** remains a must-start (71.42) despite facing Zac Gallen; his high base projection and favorable order placement provide enough insulation to warrant full confidence.\n\nFor the middle infield, **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) is a surprisingly strong play today. His score is bolstered significantly by a +19% SP skill advantage against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez and a rare +11% dynamic platoon edge, further aided by wind conditions that favor his profile. Conversely, **Kazuma Okamoto** (45.13) sits on the lower end of our starting threshold. While he remains in the utility slot, his value is suppressed by a difficult assignment against Nathan Eovaldi, where the SP skill deficit (-16%) largely negates the benefit of his lineup position. Among our bench options, **Chase Meidroth** (45.80) was the most difficult exclusion; his profile is nearly identical to **Kazuma Okamoto**, but the optimizer favored the higher park factor and slightly better batting order position assigned to **Kazuma Okamoto** to fill the final slot.\n\nManagement is keeping a close watch on **Caleb Durbin** (54.34), who carries a 45% rain risk heading into his matchup with Will Warren. While **Caleb Durbin** provides necessary category juice in the SB department, owners should monitor local weather updates closely to ensure he avoids a late scratch or shortened outing. Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** (46.26) remains in the lineup as a marginal start, though his sub-50 score suggests he is on the bubble; he is the most likely candidate to be bypassed if any late-breaking lineup changes force a pivot to fresher bats on the bench like **Luke Raley** or **Nelson Velazquez**.",
